==Trivia==
*Dark Dober's Japanese name, Doveru Dāku (ドヴェルダーク, Dover Dark), may be a pun on ''Dovoruzāku'' (ドヴォルザーク), the Japanese pronunciation of [[wikipedia:Dvořák|Dvořák]] - a famous Czech composer best known for composing the ''[[wikipedia:New World Symphony|New World Symphony]]''. This is supported by how Dark Dober's Japanese description mentions compositions and how most other [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sages]] are also based on historical figures.
*Dark Dober's Japanese description may have been inspired by [[wikipedia:Mamoru Samuragochi|Mamoru Samuragochi]], a composer who was once hailed as "the Beethoven of Japan", but eventually confessed to having a ghostwriter write his best-known compositions for him. Samuragochi also used to have shoulder-length hair vaguely like Dark Dober's.
*Given the musical theming, the shape and animation of Dark Dober's tail may be intended to resemble a conductor's baton.

